# Private reference material. The repository root is published by GitHub Pages,
# so anything committed under SLiVR/ becomes publicly fetchable. These paths
# hold the scanned scouting book, the unpublished paper, the research-mode text
# and the location workbook with venue contacts.
#
# docs/* excludes the contents rather than the directory itself, because git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded.
docs/*
outputs/

# The living verification record is deliberately published. It carries test
# procedures and execution history that must survive in source control, and it
# contains no private reference material.
!docs/FULL-SYSTEM-TESTING.md
!docs/CATALOG_COORDINATE_UPDATES_2026-09-20.md

# Optional runtime configuration: provider credentials never enter committed source.
config/runtime.js
